3. OPEN-SOURCE COMPONENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Writ Desktop bundles third-party open-source software. Each such component is
licensed under its own terms, which are reproduced in full in
`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` in this repository and shipped inside the application
(Settings → About → Open-source licences). Where a component's licence grants
you rights broader than this Agreement, that licence governs that component.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. UPDATES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The application may check for and install updates. Every update is verified
against a signing key compiled into the application before it is applied; an
update that does not verify is refused. Automatic updates can be disabled in the
application's settings, and managed deployments can point the application at an
internal update feed or disable updates entirely.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. DATA
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Writ Desktop is local-first. Your workflows, credentials, and run results are
stored on your own machine. Nothing is transmitted to Writ unless you explicitly
link a cloud account or opt in to diagnostics. See `SECURITY.md` for the precise,
bounded description of what is and is not protected, and what is and is not sent.

